<Concept title="Dodge" section="Mechanics">
  <p>The key words <strong>MUST</strong>, <strong>MUST NOT</strong>, <strong>SHOULD</strong>, and <strong>MAY</strong> are used as in RFC 2119.</p>

  <p>A committed roll in the <em>steering</em> direction at the moment the dodge is admitted. Dodge is <strong>free</strong> — no stamina or resource cost — so its balancing cost is <em>commitment</em>: the full 41-frame action must play out, its displacement curve is front-loaded, and it grants <strong>no damage immunity</strong> — the roll is safe because it moves the player and passes through bodies, not because hits whiff (see <a href={siteUrl('/states/player-state')}>Player State Machine → Action commitment</a>).</p>

  <h2>Phases and timing (30 fps action clock)</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Phase</th><th>Window</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><strong>Pass-through</strong></td><td>frames 0–9 (0.33 s)</td><td>Body contact disabled: the rolling player passes through enemies and push bodies; contact-based charge stops do not register.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Roll</strong></td><td>frames 0–19</td><td>Displacement follows the original root-motion curve (see below); the visual clip is the weapon-set's <code>&lt;prefix&gt;_esc_f</code>.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Get-up</strong></td><td>frames 20–40</td><td>Root motion decays to a small forward drift then a settle-back to the final root; fully vulnerable; contact re-enabled from frame 10.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><strong>Completion</strong></td><td>frame 41</td><td>Logical position snaps to the final drawn root; the idle or run loop attaches immediately with no blend.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <ul>
    <li>The action <strong>MUST</strong> last 41 frames (1.367 s), weapon-independent — the extracted <code>_esc_f</code> clip (20 frames) is the roll half only; the full action chains the get-up.</li>
    <li>Displacement <strong>MUST</strong> follow the original per-frame curve (<code>data/re_reference/player_dodge_motion.json</code>): burst over frames 2–5, a ≈1085 Q12/frame plateau through frame 13, decay to frame 25, then settle-back; total travel 17901 Q12 ≈ 4.37 u in the dodge direction (the curve's small ±x wobble is the roll arc and <strong>SHOULD</strong> be kept). A constant-velocity roll <strong>MUST NOT</strong> be used.</li>
    <li>A dodge admitted while RUNNING <strong>SHOULD</strong> add one run-speed step in the dodge direction on the admission frame (the ROM's motion integrate applies the carried run speed once before clearing it).</li>
    <li>The roll <strong>MUST</strong> stop at floor edges (the ROM's root-floor reconciliation restores the last on-floor root) — it cannot leave the floor.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Durability — the 2026-10 ROM correction</h2>
  <p><strong>There are no dodge i-frames.</strong> The ROM's hit-reaction gate (<code>pszm_actor_hit</code>) excludes the knockdown/dead states (19–22, 27, 28) and the special states (23–25) — dodge (state 15) is <em>not</em> excluded: a hit at any point of the roll damages the player and interrupts the action, and a hit during states 12/15 additionally resets the actor position to the banked root. The 10-frame flag the dodge sets gates <em>body contact</em> (the roll-through), not damage. <em>History: #273 gave the roll the whole move phase as i-frames; #377 tightened it to a fixed 0.2 s window; the decoded ROM removes damage immunity entirely — the pass-through window replaces it.</em></p>
  <ul>
    <li><code>take_damage</code> during DODGING <strong>MUST</strong> apply damage and interrupt (DODGING → DAMAGED/DOWN) at every frame of the action, exactly as when idle.</li>
    <li>For the first 10 frames, enemy body contact and contact-based reactions <strong>MUST</strong> pass through the rolling player (a charging enemy does not stop on the roll).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Admission</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>A dodge input while ATTACKING or DODGING <strong>MUST</strong> be ignored — the current action commits first (busy-press replay case).</li>
    <li>Holding the dodge button <strong>MUST NOT</strong> chain rolls — one roll per press (held-no-repeat replay case).</li>
    <li>A dodge <strong>MUST NOT</strong> be admitted within 10 frames of the previous admission (the tick gate) or during the 15-frame spawn/scene warmup.</li>
    <li>The dodge direction <strong>MUST</strong> be the steering held entering the press frame: while running, the current movement direction; while idle, the facing. A direction pressed on the same frame as the dodge <strong>MUST NOT</strong> redirect it (simultaneous-turn replay case).</li>
    <li>Starting a dodge <strong>MUST</strong> drop an in-progress technique charge.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reference</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>data/re_reference/player_dodge_motion.json</code> — the 41-frame displacement curve (rerun: <code>scripts/tools/dump_player_dodge_motion.py --evidence &lt;pszm-decomp&gt;/native/evidence/player-dodge-frame-rom.json</code>).</li>
    <li><code>pszm-decomp</code> <code>native/runtime/player_frame.c</code> (admission gates, 41-frame action clock, completion attach), <code>native/runtime/action_animation.c</code> (motion 3 length), <code>native/runtime/actor_hit.c</code> (state-15 hit reaction — no immunity), <code>player-dodge-frame-rom.json</code> / <code>player-dodge-input-rom.json</code> (ROM replays: 41-frame timeline, root trace, admission cases).</li>
    <li>The in-repo <code>dodge-debug</code> tool (web mock at <code>#/dodge-debug</code>) visualized the authored i-frame model — retained for history, superseded by this page.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Implemented by</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>scripts/3d/player/player.gd</code> (Player) — <code>_start_dodge</code> guards commitment and cooldown, caches the steering direction, and seeds the roll with one run-speed step when admitted from RUNNING; <code>_handle_dodge</code> steps the ROM displacement curve per frame with the floor edge check; completion snaps to the final root and returns to IDLE; <code>take_damage</code> treats DODGING like IDLE (no immunity window); the pass-through window gates contact-based interactions.</li>
  </ul>

  <p><a href={siteUrl('/mechanics')}>← Mechanics</a></p>
</Concept>
